      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\frac{6x-4}{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Splitting the fraction into separate terms and then simplifying the fractions in the individual terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6x-4}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{6x}{2}-\\frac{4}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{6}{2}\\cdot x-\\frac{4}{2} & = \\\\ 3x-2 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
